  "title": "The principle asks what existing things must do",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "6d771385-ad81-465e-b5a4-fe39186536bd",
      "text": "Most theories in biology ask what things must do in order to exist. The free energy principle inverts this and asks what a thing must do, given that it exists as a thing distinct from its surroundings.",
